\\ A peer image's program: it serves the remote effect Ledger (EFFECTS.md §12.12).
\\
\\ (serve Ledger ...) gives one implementation for each operation of the effect.
\\ The peer's runtime runs one of them for each request it acts on, in a
\\ transaction: what the implementation writes is kept aside while it runs, and
\\ when it returns, its writes and the record of the request (its key, its
\\ argument and this reply) are committed in one durable step, and only then is
\\ the reply sent. A request key that already has a record is answered from the
\\ record, or refused as a conflict if its argument differs, without running
\\ anything. If the implementation traps, nothing is committed and nothing is
\\ replied.
\\
\\ The store is a map from I64 to I64, reached through two effects the runtime
\\ provides: (perform StoreRead get cell) and (perform StoreWrite put cell value).
\\ A cell never written reads 0, and a read sees what this request has written.
\\
\\   cell 0   the total
\\   cell 1   the number of additions
\\   cell 2   the request key of the latest addition
\\
\\ total is declared read-only, so its implementation may not perform
\\ StoreWrite, directly or through anything it calls: the program would be
\\ rejected. add returns the pair its caller expects: status 0 and the new total.
\\
\\ This program has no main and does not run alone (sh frontend/fenrir.sh run
\\ refuses it): tools/solo5/remote-build.mjs builds the peer image of
\\ harness/run-tc1-remote-run.sh from this file.

(include "ledger.decl.fen")

(define bump {(Tuple I64 I64) --> Unit}
  cell by -> (perform StoreWrite put cell (+ (perform StoreRead get cell) by)))

(serve Ledger
  ((add key amount) -> (do (bump 0 amount)
                           (bump 1 1)
                           (perform StoreWrite put 2 key)
                           (tuple 0 (perform StoreRead get 0))))
  ((total u) -> (perform StoreRead get 0)))
